WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:07.930
Earlier this week Council held its monthly
meeting for April.

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:11.890
With the Draft Long Term Plan currently in
public consultation, it’s a busy time for

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:15.240
Council and there was a large agenda to get through.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:20.740
The Council works closely with Te Ngāi Tūāhuriri Rūnanga on many significant issues around our district.

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:25.420
A proposal was made that a seat with voting rights be made available on the District Planning

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:29.680
and Regulation Committee, in order that the
Rūnanga could contribute to a review of the

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:31.820
Waimakariri District Plan.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:35.570
Although this motion was narrowly defeated,
the Council will continue to look at ways

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:39.020
it can partner with Ngāi Tūāhuriri to develop
our district.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:46.290
Council appointed Councillors Atkinson, Meyer
and Doody to the hearing and deliberations

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:51.280
panel for the review of the local Alcohol
Policy and the hearing and deliberations panel

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.580
for Liquor Ban Bylaw review.

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:56.240
These hearings are scheduled to take place
over July.

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:02.990
The Council also formally adopted the final
Waimakariri District Development Strategy,

00:01:02.990 --> 00:01:06.840
Our District, Our Future – Waimakariri 2048.

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:11.600
This document was presented to the community
last year for feedback and will help guide

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:14.840
our growing district’s development over
the next 30 years.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:21.760
Councillors also had to consider a number
of complex water and wastewater infrastructure

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:23.860
issues and as a result.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:28.689
Brought forward funding for improving wastewater
services in the Tuahiwi area.

00:01:28.689 --> 00:01:32.609
Brought forward funding and approved staff
proceeding with physical works on the upgrade

00:01:32.609 --> 00:01:38.040
of the Oxford Rural No. 1 water scheme while
waiting for a resource consent to be granted.

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:43.200
And approved a new budget for drainage work
in Springbrook in order to mitigate flooding.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:50.740
The Councillors also planned for the upcoming
Anzac Day commemorations and they will attend

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:53.160
the following services across the district:

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:11.600
The next monthly Council meeting will be at
the Council Chambers in Rangiora on Tuesday

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:13.600
1st of May at 1pm.

